  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** MaxCyte’s operations are experiencing broad-based revenue contraction, with softer demand across both core consumables/instruments and Strategic Platform License program-related income. The company hit the top of previously reduced preliminary ranges, suggesting some stabilization but no return to growth. End-market interest in cell-therapy enabling technologies appears to be moderating near term, as fewer new programs and milestones materialize. The broader cell-engineering field still advances, yet MaxCyte’s near-term adoption trajectory reflects a breather rather than acceleration.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is emphasizing cost discipline and cash preservation, trimming operating expenses and improving gross margins to protect the balance sheet. Guidance for the coming year anticipates continued core-revenue softness, offset only partially by moderately higher SPL-related contributions—a cautious posture that signals realism over optimism. With a strong cash runway and limited projected burn, management is positioning the company to weather the revenue trough without immediate financing risk, though the market has yet to see a concrete plan to reignite top-line momentum.",
